        "header": "3Mind2Act World Benchmark",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.26444/2611.26444v1/figures/capability_map/background.jpg",
                "caption": "Figure 1:All 30 tasks, grouped by view and capability.Mindtasks emphasize decisions based on historical observation,Acttasks precise and timely physical execution, andMind2Acttasks the closed-loop composition of the two, in which action outcomes guide subsequent decisions. Each view has ten tasks, and together they cover twelve capability categories and five application domains. The central wheel groups the capability categories by view; the surrounding tiles show each task’s ID and scene, framed by view. Each task has three difficulty levels and two scene settings (CleanandRandom), giving 180 configurations.",
                "position": 1434
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.26444/2611.26444v1/m2a_wordmark.png",
                "caption": "",
                "position": 1435
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.26444/2611.26444v1/figures/process_difficulty/background.jpg",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Difficult steps inside eight Hard-level tasks.Each panel follows one Hard-level demonstration through four intermediate steps and shows what makes each step hard: the bold label under a frame names the operation, and the italic line the demand that makes it difficult. A failure at any of these steps blocks the stages after it. The color of the task ID gives its view, and the tag beside the task name the Hard-level setting; Fig.3compares the levels themselves.",
                "position": 1693
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.26444/2611.26444v1/figures/difficulty_levels/background.jpg",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Easy, Medium and Hard levels of twelve tasks.Four tasks per view atEasy,MediumandHard. A harder level keeps the goal and raises one or more task demands:Mindtasks add more to remember or infer,Acttasks require more spatial accuracy and physical stability, andMind2Acttasks lengthen the workflow or shorten the response window. The label under each frame gives the parameter that changes, and the icon beside each task name gives the kind of demand (key below the panels; its counts cover all 30 tasks).",
                "position": 1707
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.26444/2611.26444v1/figures/clean_random/CP05_0.jpg",
                "caption": "Figure 4:Examples of the Clean and Random settings.Every task is evaluated in both settings; shown are the first head-camera frames of three example tasks.Cleanscenes use default materials and lighting without clutter, and eachRandomslot adds clutter and varies surfaces and lighting (dots: table color, light tint) while keeping the task’s objects, targets and events.",
