                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.26444/2611.26444v1/figures/evaluation_loop/demo_1.jpg",
                "caption": "Figure 5:Training, evaluation and diagnosis pipeline.Training: end-to-end policies are fine-tuned on 4,500 demonstrations generated by scripted experts.Evaluation: the policies predict action chunks and the agents call motion tools, while the evaluator decides success from simulator state hidden from both.Diagnosis: episode logs feed a model profile card, which records where each failed episode first breaks down and whether the failure lies inMind,Actor their composition (Section6.1). Dashed elements are the next stage of the loop. The failure codes on a card become concrete changes (Table7), and the improved model is evaluated again (Section7). The evaluation and diagnosis panels trace one recorded GPT-6 Astra episode on S1 Medium, and the card panel is illustrative.",
